{
  "version": "1.1",
  "verified_on": "2026-09-22",
  "about": "Queries whose widely-cited answer is verifiably outdated. Each trap names the old answer (still all over blogs, Stack Overflow and model training data), the answer that is current, and where the change is documented. An engine passes a trap when it surfaces the current answer AND marks the old one as outdated; repeating the old answer with no warning is the failure this task set exists to measure. Traps with cohort \"recent\" changed between August 2025 and March 2026, after most models' training data was gathered: a model can't answer them from memory, so they are the ones where retrieval has to do the work.",
